==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries.als
    rationale: Removing the uniqueness constraint on (forApp, eventType, actor) triples allows the model to create two ApplicationEvents that share the same application+eventType+actor, representing an in-place mutation/replacement. The AppendOnly predicate detects this via the 'no two distinct events share the same triple' clause, which will then find a counterexample.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_016_AuditTrailComplete
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_016_AuditTrailComplete: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_OnePendingPerCustomer  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_OnePendingPerCustomer.als
    rationale: Removing the at-most-one-pending constraint allows the model to construct two LoanApplications with the same owner both in PendingReview status. The FR_005_OnePendingPerCustomer predicate will find this as a counterexample.
    expected to FAIL: FR_005_OnePendingPerCustomer
      - FR_005_OnePendingPerCustomer: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_LeastPrivilege  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_LeastPrivilege.als
    rationale: Removing the LeastPrivilege enforcement fact allows the model to create an Operation where a Customer successfully calls OpPostDecision (outcome = OutSuccess), violating the permission matrix. The LeastPrivilege predicate's implication 'OutSuccess implies in Allowed' catches this.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, FR_015_StaffOnlyDecideAndAudit
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_015_StaffOnlyDecideAndAudit: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_NoInformationLeakage  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_NoInformationLeakage.als
    rationale: Removing the NoInformationLeakage fact allows the model to construct an Operation where a Customer calls GetAppByRef on another customer's application and receives OutDenied instead of OutNotFound, leaking existence information. The predicate checks for OutNotFound specifically.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_013_CustomerSeesOnlyOwnApps
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_013_CustomerSeesOnlyOwnApps: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AuditDecisionEvent  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_AuditDecisionEvent.als
    rationale: Removing the fact that every decided application must have exactly one decision audit event allows the model to have an Approved application with no ApprovedEvt ApplicationEvent. The AuditCompleteness and FR_016_AuditTrailComplete predicates both check for the existence of that event and will find a counterexample.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_016_AuditTrailComplete, AttributionCorrectness
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_016_AuditTrailComplete: FAIL (expected)
      - AttributionCorrectness: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AtMostOneDecision  → runs/A-L1/mutated_F_AtMostOneDecision.als
    rationale: Removing the at-most-one-decision constraint allows two distinct Decision records to point to the same LoanApplication, representing a race condition where two concurrent staff decisions both succeed. The ConcurrencySafety and FR_012_ConcurrentDecisionRejected predicates both enforce lone/no duplicate decisions per application.
    expected to FAIL: ConcurrencySafety, FR_012_ConcurrentDecisionRejected
      - ConcurrencySafety: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_012_ConcurrentDecisionRejected: PASS (vacuous?)

